  "title": "OpenBMI SSVEP EEG dataset (Lee et al. 2019)",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted derivative dataset of steady-state visually evoked potential (SSVEP) EEG recordings from 54 subjects across 2 sessions, containing 21,600 trials acquired at 1000 Hz sampling rate with 62 channels. This dataset, derived from the Lee et al. 2019 source dataset, has been standardized using the Mother of All BCI Benchmarks (MOABB) framework to enable reproducible benchmarking of brain-computer interface paradigms based on SSVEP stimulation.",
  "methods_description": "EEG recordings from 54 subjects with 62-channel acquisition at 1000 Hz sampling frequency. Data collected across 2 sessions with SSVEP stimulation paradigm, yielding 4-second trial epochs across 4 classes. Original data collection methods detailed in the primary publication (Lee et al. 2019).",
